# General safety net: an eprot/ checkpoint dir under any tests_rate* sweep
# results dir should always be local-only, per every sweep in this project
# (see DEVLOG.txt). Added after the refine sweep's checkpoints briefly got
# committed because the specific rule above was added one commit too late
# -- this catches any future sweep directory even if a specific line is
# forgotten again.
softmax/monte_carlo/tests_rate*/**/eprot/

# Plots (plot_run.py, plot_structural_metrics.py, identify_k_sites.py) are
# generated locally from data.dat/eprot checkpoints -- local-only for the
# same reason eprot/ itself is: regeneratable from data already gitignored,
# and PNGs would bloat the repo the same way the accidental eprot/ commit
# did. Also covers structural_metrics.csv (compute_structural_metrics.py's
# output) -- cheap to regenerate from a *.pt checkpoint set that's itself
# never committed, so keeping the CSV out too avoids a committed artifact
# whose source can't be reproduced from what's actually in the repo.
*.png
softmax/monte_carlo/**/structural_metrics.csv
softmax/monte_carlo/k_sites_plots/
